# data/energy.json is regenerated hourly by the fetch, so a conflict on it is
# never a disagreement worth resolving - it is two snapshots written an hour
# apart, and the next run overwrites whichever survives.
#
# "-merge" was the wrong tool: it marks the file binary and makes git REFUSE
# to merge, which produces the hand-resolved conflict it was meant to avoid.
# "merge=ours" keeps the version already on the branch and needs the driver
# below, which git will not invent for itself:
#
#   git config merge.ours.driver true
#
# That is a local setting, so deploy/install-git.sh sets it too.
data/energy.json merge=ours -diff
